// Single-worker textbook-scatter schedule for 19-histogram-unconstrained
// (TASK-0432 AC#2). Mirrors 08-histogram/schedules/textbook.sched.nuc:
// drives `prog.textbook.algo.nuc` (selected via `schedule for`,
// TASK-0049.03; `kernels.textbook.rs` paired by the variant rule,
// TASK-0049.08).
//
// Single worker (`host`): the data-dependent WRITE
// `histogram[bucket(input[i])]` needs the whole of `histogram` mutable on
// one worker, trivially satisfied (no transfers, no cross-worker bin
// fan-in). `bucket` is placed on the same worker — a pure index-computing
// kernel called inline at the scatter site. UNLIKE 08-histogram, THIS
// example's `input.bin` carries values outside `[0, BINS)`, so `bucket()`
// does REAL runtime work and the output is bit-identical to `reference.bin`
// (computed THROUGH the modulo) only if the compiled index path evaluates
// the kernel.

schedule for "../prog.textbook.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place bucket      on host;
    place inc         on host;

    // No loop transforms, no transfer directives (single worker).
}
